# The C library resident in B2: its functions, by number. A number
# never changes and is never used again, new ones go at the end, so a
# program keeps working with a newer CLIB.SYS. Each line: the number, the
# name a program calls, the signature (clib/marshal.c), and the
# library's function when it has another name.
